.Dd September 23, 2026
.Dt PKG6REPO 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg6repo
.Nd manage local IPS package repositories
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm create
.Op Fl -repo-version Ar 4
.Ar path
.Nm
.Cm add-publisher
.Fl s Ar repo
.Ar publisher ...
.Nm
.Cm remove-publisher
.Op Fl n
.Fl s Ar repo
.Ar publisher ...
.Nm
.Cm get
.Fl s Ar repo
.Op Fl F Ar format
.Op Fl H
.Op Ar name ...
.Nm
.Cm set
.Fl s Ar repo
.Ar section/property Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Nm
.Cm info
.Fl s Ar repo
.Op Fl F Ar format
.Op Fl H
.Op Fl p Ar publisher ...
.Nm
.Cm list
.Fl s Ar repo
.Op Fl F Ar format
.Op Fl H
.Op Fl p Ar publisher ...
.Op Ar pattern ...
.Nm
.Cm contents
.Fl s Ar repo
.Op Fl t Ar type ...
.Op Fl p Ar publisher ...
.Op Ar pattern ...
.Nm
.Cm search
.Fl s Ar repo
.Op Fl F Ar format
.Op Fl H
.Op Fl p Ar publisher
.Op Fl n Ar limit
.Ar query
.Nm
.Cm rebuild | refresh
.Fl s Ar repo
.Op Fl p Ar publisher
.Op Fl -no-index
.Nm
.Cm import-pkg5
.Fl s Ar source
.Fl d Ar repo
.Op Fl p Ar publisher ...
.Op Fl -adopt-existing
.Op Fl -max-archive-entries Ar n
.Op Fl -max-extract-bytes Ar n
.Nm
.Cm list-obsoleted | search-obsoleted | show-obsoleted |
.Cm restore-obsoleted | export-obsoleted
.Fl s Ar repo
.Fl p Ar publisher
.Ar ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility creates and maintains IPS package repositories on the local file
system.
The
.Xr pkg6depotd 8
depot serves them read-only over HTTP; there is no remote administration.
Every
.Ar repo ,
.Ar path
and
.Ar source
operand is a file system path.
A URI, including a
.Pa file://
URI, is rejected.
.Pp
A subcommand either does what it reports or exits non-zero.
Unknown publishers, unsupported properties and existing output files are
detected before anything is changed.
.Pp
The
.Fl F
option selects
.Cm table
(the default),
.Cm json
or
.Cm tsv
output.
.Fl H
omits the header line.
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm create Oo Fl -repo-version Ar 4 Oc Ar path
Create a repository.
Version 4 is the only format.
Fails if
.Ar path
already holds
.Pa pkg6.repository
or
.Pa pkg5.repository .
.It Cm add-publisher Fl s Ar repo Ar publisher ...
Add publishers.
The first publisher of a repository becomes its default publisher.
Fails, adding none, if a publisher already exists or is named twice.
.It Cm remove-publisher Oo Fl n Oc Fl s Ar repo Ar publisher ...
Remove publishers with their catalogs and package manifests.
Fails, removing none, if a publisher does not exist.
With
.Fl n ,
print what would be removed and change nothing.
.It Cm get Fl s Ar repo Oo Ar name ... Oc
Print repository properties, optionally only the named sections or
.Ar section/property
names.
The properties are
.Sy publisher/prefix ,
the default publisher, and
.Sy repository/version .
Any other name is an error.
.It Cm set Fl s Ar repo Ar section/property Ns = Ns Ar value ...
Set properties.
Only
.Sy publisher/prefix
can be set, to a configured publisher.
All operands are checked before anything changes.
.It Cm info Fl s Ar repo Op Fl p Ar publisher ...
Print the package count, status and last update time of each publisher,
or of the given publishers.
.It Cm list Fl s Ar repo Oo Fl p Ar publisher ... Oc Op Ar pattern ...
List package versions, including obsolete ones.
A
.Ar pattern
is a glob
.Pq Sq * , Sq \&?
matched against the whole package name.
All publishers and patterns given are used.
If a pattern matches nothing, the other matches are printed and the
command exits 1.
.It Cm contents Fl s Ar repo Oo Fl t Ar type ... Oc Oo Fl p Ar publisher ... Oc Op Ar pattern ...
Print one line per file, directory, link, dependency and license of the
matching packages.
A
.Ar pattern
is a regular expression matched against the package name.
.Ar type
is one of
.Cm file ,
.Cm dir ,
.Cm link ,
.Cm depend
or
.Cm license .
Unmatched patterns are handled as by
.Cm list .
.It Cm search Fl s Ar repo Oo Fl p Ar publisher Oc Oo Fl n Ar limit Oc Ar query
Search the package index.
Without
.Fl p ,
the default publisher is searched, or every publisher if there is no
default.
.It Cm rebuild | refresh Fl s Ar repo Oo Fl p Ar publisher Oc Op Fl -no-index
Rebuild the catalog and the search index, which is part of it, from the
package manifests.
The two subcommands are the same.
.Fl -no-index
is accepted for pkg5 scripts and has no effect.
On a repository managed by
.Cm import-pkg5
the result is published as a new generation.
.It Cm import-pkg5 Fl s Ar source Fl d Ar repo Op Fl p Ar publisher ...
Import a pkg5 repository directory or
.Pa .p5p
archive.
All packages of the selected publishers, by default all in
.Ar source ,
become visible in one generation switch, or none do.
Importing an archive that was already imported changes nothing.
An exact FMRI that is already published with a different manifest rejects
the whole import.
.Fl -adopt-existing
converts a repository in the older layout; run it while readers are
stopped.
.It Cm list-obsoleted , search-obsoleted Fl q Ar regex , show-obsoleted Fl f Ar fmri
Inspect the legacy obsoleted store, which earlier pkg6 builds filled with
package versions moved out of the catalog.
These subcommands do not change the catalog or packages; opening a
non-empty store may rewrite its own index under
.Pa obsoleted/ .
.It Cm restore-obsoleted Fl s Ar repo Fl p Ar publisher Fl f Ar fmri Op Fl -no-rebuild
Publish a store entry's manifest into the repository and then remove the
entry.
Not supported on repositories managed by
.Cm import-pkg5 .
.It Cm export-obsoleted Fl s Ar repo Fl p Ar publisher Fl o Ar file Op Fl q Ar regex
Write matching store entries to a new JSON
.Ar file .
Fails, writing nothing, if
.Ar file
exists or nothing matches.
.El
.Sh OBSOLETE PACKAGES
To obsolete a package, publish a new version whose manifest sets
.Sy pkg.obsolete=true .
It stays in the catalog, where
.Xr pkg 1
clients see it.
The obsoleted store is not obsoletion and not retirement.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
The command completed.
.It 1
An error occurred, or a pattern matched nothing.
.It 2
Invalid command line, including a URI where a path is required.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a repository for the depot and add a publisher:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# pkg6repo create /var/pkg6depotd/repo
# pkg6repo add-publisher -s /var/pkg6depotd/repo openindiana.org
.Ed
.Pp
Import a pkg5 archive:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# pkg6repo import-pkg5 -s userland.p5p -d /var/pkg6depotd/repo
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkg 1 ,
.Xr pkg6depotd 8
.Sh NOTES
The pkg5 subcommands and options that
.Nm
does not implement are rejected, among them remote repositories,
.Fl -key ,
.Fl -cert ,
.Cm set Fl p ,
.Cm contents Fl m
and
.Cm rebuild Fl -no-catalog .
